M8 x main integration, 2026-10-12: merge resolution notes
==========================================================

Merge commit a6985e1: origin/main 597d1a5 (PR #18, bundle split) into
codex/m8-favorites b0de846 (M8 favorites and recent searches). Merge
base f5382bd. Git reported six content conflicts; the resolution kept
both branches' behaviour everywhere, as required.

Conflicts and resolutions
-------------------------

1. apps/web/src/presentation/App.tsx
   Kept main's structure: lazy MedicationSearchPage and
   MedicationDetailPage behind one Suspense with the calm RouteLoading
   placeholder, the pathname-keyed RouteErrorBoundary, the
   RouteFocusContext provider with the pending-focus effect, and the
   focusable static headings (overview, status, route error, "Page
   unavailable"). Added M8's pieces into that structure: the
   preferences prop on the search and detail routes, the /favorites
   route and its nav link, and LocalPreferencesSettings at the end of
   /status. FavoritesPage and LocalPreferencesSettings import EAGERLY,
   with a comment stating why: the precache is one asset below its
   sixteen-asset cap, and one more lazy chunk would take the last slot,
   so both small pages ride in the entry chunk. Verified after the
   merge by npm run build: 174 modules, entry chunk 89.41 kB (up from
   main's 78.07 kB), largest chunk framework-vendor 258.58 kB, 9 JS
   chunks + 1 stylesheet, 15 precached assets (cap 16), and
   apps/web/pwa/build-output.test.ts passes (every chunk under 500,000
   bytes, every JS/CSS asset precached, at most 16 assets).

2. apps/web/src/presentation/MedicationSearchPage.tsx
   Both branches fixed the same stale debounced URL write. Kept ONE
   implementation, main's naming, with both branches' guarantees:
   setSearchParamsRef + [query]-only dependencies + the pathname guard
   (identical on both sides; main's fuller comment retained), main's
   onActivate prop firing on click AND on Enter, and M8's handler
   recordOpenedSearch, which calls cancelQueryUrlSync() before
   recording the recent search - so activating a result cancels the
   pending URL write AND records the recent search, from both the
   mouse and the keyboard path. The page calls useRouteHeadingFocus()
   (main) and keeps M8's preferences prop, recent-searches panel,
   queryRevision bookkeeping and the ConfirmationDialog with its
   headingRef fallback focus.

3. apps/web/src/presentation/MedicationDetailPage.tsx
   Kept M8's favorite toggle (FavoriteViewState keyed by product id,
   aria-pressed toggle, per-write notices) and the preferences prop,
   plus main's useRouteHeadingFocus() and the route-loading placeholder
   check inside focusWasMoved (auto-merged from main).

4. apps/web/src/presentation/App.test.tsx
   Union: M8's preferences mock and services field, M8's
   "registers favorites as a route in navigation" (which also asserts
   the favorites heading receives focus after the nav click - section 3
   of the brief), and main's findByRole rewrites for lazy routes plus
   its two focus tests ("focuses the search heading once the lazy
   route chunk renders", "keeps focus where a user moved it while a
   lazy route was loading") and the waitFor hardening of the detail
   focus assertion. No assertion was dropped.

5. apps/web/src/presentation/MedicationSearchPage.test.tsx
   Union. Both branches wrote the same PathnameProbe/locationPath
   helpers and vi.restoreAllMocks - identical, merged once. Both
   branches' regression tests for the stale URL write are KEPT BOTH
   (the brief allows duplicates that do not conflict): M8's "does not
   let a pending query URL update undo opening a result" (records the
   recent search through the override) and main's "drops a pending
   query URL write when a result is opened"; main's variant gained
   preferences={emptyPreferences()} because the merged page requires
   the preferences prop. All M8 recent-search tests and the URL-sync
   pair survive.

6. tests/browser/medication-search.spec.ts
   Both branches had made the same change (assert the search heading
   holds focus instead of main); the conflict was only main's added
   comment. Kept main's side verbatim.

Auto-merged without conflict (verified, both sides kept)
--------------------------------------------------------

- apps/web/src/Bootstrap.test.tsx: M8's preferences service mock +
  main's findByRole wait for the lazy search page.
- apps/web/src/presentation/styles.css: main's .route-loading and
  .route-error + M8's favorites, recent-searches, settings and
  dialog styles.
- docs/MILESTONE_7_EVIDENCE.md: main's bundle-split follow-up section;
  M8 never touched it.
- Evidence folders are disjoint per branch
  (bundle-split-2026-10-09 vs milestone-8-2026-10-09); both kept.
- apps/web/pwa/worker.ts, worker.test.ts, vite.config.ts, build-output
  .test.ts, route-focus.ts, route-recovery.test.tsx: from main only.

Fix-ups required by the union
-----------------------------

- apps/web/src/presentation/route-recovery.test.tsx (main's new file):
  its AppServices literal lacked preferences, which M8's AppServices
  requires. Added preferences: unavailablePreferencesService - the
  documented seam for isolated view tests; the recovery route's chunk
  fails before any preferences call, so no behaviour changed.

- The favorites heading focus (brief section 3) needed NO extra work:
  the page is eager, so the App pathname effect finds its
  h1[tabindex="-1"] in the same commit and focuses it directly.
  M8's existing App.test.tsx case asserts exactly this and passes on
  the merged tree, so the optional useRouteHeadingFocus() fallback in
  FavoritesPage was not needed and the optional commit
  "fix(web): focus the favorites heading on navigation" was not
  created.

Verification on the merged tree (before the /favorites PWA work)
----------------------------------------------------------------

npm run typecheck exit 0; npm run lint exit 0; prettier --check exit 0
after wrapping one JSX attribute; vitest run: 61 files, 967 tests,
0 failures; npm run build exit 0 with no chunk-size warning;
apps/web/pwa/build-output.test.ts 3 passed.

Toolchain caveat (recording environment): the worker shell exports
uppercase env names (SYSTEMROOT/WINDIR), and Node worker threads read
their env copy case-sensitively, so os.tmpdir()'s Windows-directory
fallback resolved relative to the repo and
tests/importer/artifact.test.ts "builds under the OS temp directory"
failed spuriously. Re-exporting canonical-case SystemRoot/windir (and
unsetting the uppercase duplicates) restored the canonical
Windows temporary-directory behavior and the test passes; no test was changed.
Playwright 1.63.0 browsers (chromium-1243, webkit-2359) were
reinstalled after the host session restart wiped the browser cache.

Offline /favorites (brief section 2) red/green evidence lives in
integration-worker-red.log, integration-worker-green.log,
integration-browser-red.log and integration-browser-green.log in this
folder; the full-check log is integration-full-check.log.
